WEBVTT

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:46.940
JOBS

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:52.440
This is so cool. Our own place!

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:55.820
That's right. Our own store.

00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:57.070
All right!

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:03.040
Now we don't have to do any more jobs
for the Company. Right, Tsukasa?

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:04.830
Actually, about that...

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:06.370
Welcome to Fish &amp; Fish!

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:08.960
Oh. It's you, Katsuragi.

00:02:09.290 --> 00:02:10.920
Not much of a welcome,

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:15.710
especially when I'm bringing you a job
to celebrate the opening of your store.

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:18.220
Hey, this is a smoke-free store!

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:21.760
And we're not gonna do any more
of the Company's jobs.

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:24.720
I'm afraid we have no choice, Hiroki.

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:31.020
Of course you don't. Who do you think
paid for this store and everything in it?

00:02:31.270 --> 00:02:35.980
I have to pay the Company back
by doing jobs for them.

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:40.240
But I told you I wouldn't work
for them anymore.

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:44.740
I didn't say you had to. I'll do
the Company's jobs by myself.

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:46.410
Tsukasa...

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:50.170
You take care of our store
while I'm gone, okay?

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.750
O...Okay.

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:53.960
Wait!

00:02:54.670 --> 00:02:57.260
Promise me you won't go in with Satoru.

00:02:57.630 --> 00:03:00.010
I won't. I promise.

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:15.270
Mr. Sakamoto, when can we see you again?

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:18.490
Won't be too long.

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:21.780
Till then, here's some pocket money.

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:24.160
Thank you so much!

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:28.500
Come back soon! We'll be waiting!

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:34.330
You got a problem?

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:38.670
It's Inui.

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:46.560
Wait, Inui. Give this message to Satomi.

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:50.310
Tell him it wasn't my idea,
it was the Chinese Embassy...

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:01.490
That bastard Sakamoto.
His leg's shattered, apparently.

00:04:02.990 --> 00:04:04.610
You did well, Inui.

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:06.830
I did well.

00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:09.830
This should save us some face
with the Chens.

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:13.750
It shows we're committed to
rooting out any traitors.

00:04:14.830 --> 00:04:17.340
Welcome to Japan, President Chen.

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:20.880
I assume you know why I'm here.

00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:23.840
My father and grandfather are furious.

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:27.470
So that's the young hotshot
of the Chen Group.

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:29.640
Looks like a moron to me.

00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:35.150
Dahao, we'll deal with any problems
that occur among us yakuza,

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:37.610
but the traitor at the embassy is...

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:42.280
I'm sure Zhou has his reasons.
If I talk to him, he'll come around.

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:44.860
You're not to lay a finger on him.
Understand?

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:50.990
"GUPPIES 10 YEN"

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:52.620
So cheap!

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:55.670
Ten yen for a guppy. What a deal!

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:57.630
For a guppy? You sure?

00:04:57.920 --> 00:04:59.880
That's right. Ten yen.

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:05.260
They're cheap so people
buy them on impulse.

00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:08.640
'Cause if they buy one, they'll need
something to keep it in too.

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:12.600
The guppies are just cheap bait
to get people to buy tanks.

00:05:12.850 --> 00:05:16.020
Then once they have a tank,
they'll start wanting expensive fish too.

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:20.020
My friend thought it up.
Pretty neat idea, huh?

00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:23.030
You sure you should be
telling customers that?

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:26.950
Well, I'm buying some anyway.
Two of them.

00:05:27.110 --> 00:05:28.160
What? Really?

00:05:28.450 --> 00:05:31.740
But no tank. I've already got one at home.

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:33.910
Oh, you've got one?

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:37.920
How about taking that guy too then?

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:39.420
The arowana.

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:42.170
-It's huge!
-And way too pricey!

00:05:43.630 --> 00:05:45.170
What're you up to, Hitomi?

00:05:45.470 --> 00:05:49.590
Look Ucchi, guppies!
They're on sale for the store's opening.

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:53.850
You ain't kidding! For ten yen each,
I might buy a few to feed to Snappy.

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:55.560
I'm not selling any to you.

00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:56.730
Huh?

00:05:56.890 --> 00:06:00.060
Ucchi, it's because you said
you'd feed them to your turtle.

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:04.820
-That guy's your boyfriend?
-Err, yes.

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:15.700
Kinda ugly, don't you think?

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:20.920
Your boyfriend. Take a good look.
He's one ugly dude.

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:26.670
Come on, sell me some.
I won't use 'em for food.

00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:29.590
Give it up already. Let's go, Hitomi.

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:30.840
O...Okay.

00:06:32.510 --> 00:06:34.680
-Wait up, Hitomi.
-Stop it.

00:06:34.970 --> 00:06:37.230
-What's wrong?
-Let me go!

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:39.980
Why're you angry? What's gotten into you?

00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:41.150
Leave her alone.

00:06:41.310 --> 00:06:42.770
-Keep out of it!
-Hitomi!

00:06:42.940 --> 00:06:44.400
She told you to stop.

00:06:44.940 --> 00:06:46.480
Wait, Hitomi!

00:06:47.070 --> 00:06:48.740
Hey, wait up!

00:06:58.120 --> 00:07:01.500
Allow me to introduce Mr. Katsuragi,
one of our "employees".

00:07:01.670 --> 00:07:03.750
It is a pleasure to meet you.

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:07.010
We can speak in Japanese. My name is Zhou.

00:07:07.510 --> 00:07:09.510
That's very considerate of you.

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:14.390
The Company's control of channels in Japan
is thanks to Counselor Zhou.

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:17.600
I just chose what was most profitable.

00:07:17.810 --> 00:07:20.770
For our country and for me.

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:22.520
Excuse me.

00:07:26.150 --> 00:07:28.780
You again? What on earth do you want?

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:30.280
What do I want?

00:07:30.490 --> 00:07:32.160
Do you have any idea what you've done?

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:34.410
My father and grandfather are furious!

00:07:34.910 --> 00:07:38.580
What's that got to do with me?
I don't even know you.

00:07:38.790 --> 00:07:40.370
Cut the crap, Zhou!

00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:43.710
Is someone there with you? Is that it?

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:46.920
Okay then. Let's set up a meeting.

00:07:47.170 --> 00:07:48.760
Then we can talk directly about...

00:07:49.590 --> 00:07:50.670
Hey! Zhou!

00:07:53.010 --> 00:07:54.430
Is something wrong?

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:56.600
No, nothing.

00:07:56.810 --> 00:08:01.310
If you are having any problems,
Mr. Katsuragi will take care of them.

00:08:01.480 --> 00:08:04.060
He's well versed in that sort of thing.

00:08:04.230 --> 00:08:05.440
Leave it to me.

00:08:06.020 --> 00:08:09.280
We will protect you, Counselor.

00:08:09.530 --> 00:08:10.740
Thank you.

00:08:15.450 --> 00:08:17.450
Hey there, you like mature women?

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:19.370
We got some hot mi...

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:27.630
That was Inui, wasn't it? The guy who's
been going around beating up yakuza.

00:08:27.790 --> 00:08:30.960
I heard he killed his foster mom
when he was a kid.

00:08:31.130 --> 00:08:34.220
He's a drug dealer now, so they say.

00:08:39.510 --> 00:08:42.180
You're Inui from the Beltway Crew,
aren't you?

00:08:43.520 --> 00:08:46.690
I'm the guy with the channel
for selling uppers.

00:08:47.230 --> 00:08:48.440
Did you get my message?

00:08:49.190 --> 00:08:50.610
You're the party planner?

00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:51.860
I am.

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:56.030
I have some connections
among musicians and celebrities.

00:08:56.450 --> 00:08:58.700
I can introduce you to some hot women too.

00:08:58.870 --> 00:09:01.040
I hate women.

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:02.580
I see.

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:04.250
Anyway, let's talk.

00:09:04.540 --> 00:09:06.250
It's rather smoky in here, isn't it?

00:09:09.630 --> 00:09:10.880
Smoky, isn't it?

00:09:15.630 --> 00:09:19.140
Satomi, can you set up a meeting for me
with Zhou somehow?

00:09:19.350 --> 00:09:22.220
If I can just talk to him directly...

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:27.310
Well, that's not really
my area of expertise.

00:09:27.650 --> 00:09:29.770
If you want me to send Inui
to threaten him,

00:09:29.940 --> 00:09:32.110
then I can do that no problem.

00:09:32.570 --> 00:09:36.530
You said the counselor's wife
just had a kid, right?

00:09:36.860 --> 00:09:40.700
Hey, Inui. I want you to go and snatch
the counselor's kid.

00:09:40.990 --> 00:09:41.950
Can you do it?

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:43.160
-Yes.
-Stop!

00:09:45.500 --> 00:09:47.670
He doesn't understand Chinese.

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:50.750
But if I give him an order,
he'll never say he can't do it.

00:09:51.630 --> 00:09:54.920
So the rumors are true.
 Inui is at Satomi's beck and call.

00:09:55.470 --> 00:09:57.220
I need to go deeper.

00:09:59.260 --> 00:10:00.720
I fight for justice!

00:10:06.810 --> 00:10:10.060
5,000 yen? Is that all you've got for me?

00:10:10.230 --> 00:10:14.070
You shouldn't be charging anything
at your age! You've even got a grandkid!

00:10:14.230 --> 00:10:17.650
I do not. That child is
my daughter, Kyoko!

00:10:17.820 --> 00:10:19.160
You've lost it!

00:10:21.740 --> 00:10:23.330
Turn that off at once, Kyoko.

00:10:23.490 --> 00:10:26.080
How dare you watch a show for boys!

00:10:27.330 --> 00:10:29.210
Is that... Inui?

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:35.510
Let's try this on next.
Oh, this one's nice too.

00:10:42.390 --> 00:10:43.890
That's it. One more.

00:10:47.180 --> 00:10:49.230
-I wanna do it again!
-Okay then.

00:10:56.900 --> 00:11:00.660
-Kyoko, Kyoko!
-Stop it, you guys.

00:11:05.370 --> 00:11:06.540
Take this!

00:11:17.550 --> 00:11:18.920
Kohei...

00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:21.630
Hey, get a move on!

00:11:49.370 --> 00:11:50.750
Inui!

00:11:52.370 --> 00:11:55.290
-That guy's outta control.
-When he gets mad, he totally loses it.

00:11:55.710 --> 00:11:57.750
These all seem like
 elements of his valley.

00:11:57.920 --> 00:12:00.300
So at the bottom of this must be...

00:12:00.510 --> 00:12:02.180
What're you punks doing on our turf?

00:12:02.340 --> 00:12:04.470
Mr. Satomi, that's the guy.

00:12:05.890 --> 00:12:08.680
That's some glare you got there, kid.

00:12:09.220 --> 00:12:10.810
Use this from now on.

00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:15.360
That way even if you whack some guy,
you can claim you didn't mean to kill him.

00:12:17.860 --> 00:12:21.820
Was that all it took for Satomi
 to bring him to heel?

00:12:22.360 --> 00:12:25.200
Well, it'll make things easy for us
 at least.

00:12:27.700 --> 00:12:29.740
Who is that?

00:12:32.210 --> 00:12:34.790
Like it? It's a good bat.

00:12:34.960 --> 00:12:35.750
Yeah.

00:12:36.290 --> 00:12:37.840
A good bat.

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:40.510
You work for me now.

00:12:40.760 --> 00:12:41.760
Understood?

00:12:59.020 --> 00:13:00.440
Tsukasa...

00:13:00.820 --> 00:13:03.320
You said we were gonna run
the store together.

00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:08.910
We're too sensitive.

00:13:09.080 --> 00:13:12.080
That's why we can't make our own memories.

00:13:12.830 --> 00:13:13.960
Sensitive?

00:13:14.120 --> 00:13:18.170
It means we feel other people's emotions
 as if they were our own.

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:19.540
Huh.

00:13:19.710 --> 00:13:24.130
But if you put valleys around the peak
 I gave you, that'll lower your sensitivity

00:13:24.300 --> 00:13:28.180
and you'll be able to separate
 the outside world from your own feelings.

00:13:28.430 --> 00:13:32.850
So you need to collect lots of valleys
 to hide your peak with.

00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:37.980
Use the valleys to lock your peak away.

00:13:38.190 --> 00:13:40.110
So nobody can get at it.

00:13:40.520 --> 00:13:41.820
Lock it away?

00:13:43.650 --> 00:13:46.780
Sorry about fighting in your store
yesterday...

00:13:47.490 --> 00:13:48.870
Thanks for saving me.

00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:51.740
No big deal. Don't worry about it.

00:13:51.950 --> 00:13:55.160
Actually, I broke up with him after that.

00:13:56.250 --> 00:14:01.000
We'd been stuck in a rut anyway.
I didn't even like him that much.

00:14:01.380 --> 00:14:04.760
Anyway, today I've come
to buy that arowana. Look!

00:14:05.090 --> 00:14:06.800
-Please go.
-What?

00:14:06.970 --> 00:14:08.890
Just please leave.

00:14:10.390 --> 00:14:11.470
Give me a break.

00:14:11.640 --> 00:14:17.230
He's supposed to be Satomi's lapdog.
That's why we chose him.

00:14:17.390 --> 00:14:21.360
Now you're saying that posing as Satomi
won't get us anywhere?

00:14:21.520 --> 00:14:25.820
Satomi is definitely an element
of Inui's peak.

00:14:26.240 --> 00:14:27.780
But it's not really him.

00:14:28.280 --> 00:14:29.780
What the hell does that mean?

00:14:30.070 --> 00:14:33.870
Inui is projecting another person
onto Satomi.

00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:39.170
So it looks like Satomi, but really it's
supposed to be someone else?

00:14:39.830 --> 00:14:42.670
I'm sure it makes sense to Inui.

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:46.010
This is the masquerade he needs to create

00:14:46.170 --> 00:14:47.920
in order to survive right now.

00:14:48.300 --> 00:14:51.510
That's fine for him,
but what are we going to do?

00:14:52.220 --> 00:14:55.810
Are you saying we need to
look for another puppet?

00:14:55.970 --> 00:14:59.810
I think I have an idea of
who the real person is.

00:15:00.230 --> 00:15:03.480
When I've confirmed it,
I'll come up with an angle.

00:15:03.650 --> 00:15:06.940
Are you sure you're fine by yourself?
I could go with you.

00:15:07.690 --> 00:15:11.450
No, you can't. I promised Hiroki.

00:15:11.610 --> 00:15:14.950
Oh, right... Of course.

00:15:26.550 --> 00:15:28.840
-Party planner.
-Hello there.

00:15:30.590 --> 00:15:32.180
Do you come here often?

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:38.520
I do too.
Not getting any better though.

00:15:39.980 --> 00:15:41.140
You son of a...

00:15:45.610 --> 00:15:48.400
I said I'd come over here.

00:15:48.900 --> 00:15:51.280
Didn't I say that?

00:15:54.200 --> 00:15:58.370
You're ashamed of people seeing me?

00:15:58.830 --> 00:16:02.790
Ashamed! After all I've done for you!

00:16:02.960 --> 00:16:05.290
"PARENTS' VISITING DAY"

00:16:05.460 --> 00:16:07.960
How dare you!

00:16:13.760 --> 00:16:15.430
Is this all?

00:16:15.640 --> 00:16:20.600
After playing around with my daughter,
even getting her knocked up.

00:16:24.020 --> 00:16:27.400
Guess what, Kenta?
I got you a new bat.

00:16:27.570 --> 00:16:29.530
Thanks, Dad!

00:16:31.190 --> 00:16:32.780
Here it comes!

00:16:42.160 --> 00:16:44.710
Kenta, did you find the ball?

00:16:46.420 --> 00:16:47.460
Who's this kid?

00:16:47.630 --> 00:16:49.500
My bat!

00:16:49.710 --> 00:16:50.840
What?!

00:16:51.010 --> 00:16:53.590
Hand it over!

00:16:54.840 --> 00:16:55.970
Little brat!

00:17:00.220 --> 00:17:02.810
You took the ball as well, didn't you?

00:17:03.180 --> 00:17:04.690
Give it back, you damn thief!

00:17:09.270 --> 00:17:12.530
The thing he longed for most of all
 became his valley.

00:17:13.690 --> 00:17:15.110
In that case...

00:17:18.240 --> 00:17:20.280
Like it? It's a good bat.

00:17:20.990 --> 00:17:21.950
Yeah.

00:17:22.200 --> 00:17:23.750
A good bat.

00:17:49.900 --> 00:17:50.860
Zhou!

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:04.200
Nice shot!

00:18:08.210 --> 00:18:10.500
Zhou said to wait here.

00:18:11.130 --> 00:18:14.380
We can't meet openly, so I guess
this was the best he could do.

00:18:16.010 --> 00:18:20.930
What's got you in such a good mood?
You'd better not be high on the job.

00:18:21.720 --> 00:18:22.810
There you go.

00:18:29.730 --> 00:18:31.770
Fore!

00:18:35.440 --> 00:18:37.030
I'll go on ahead.

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:41.910
You'll have your work cut out
finding that one, Counselor.

00:18:42.070 --> 00:18:43.030
Dammit.

00:18:53.540 --> 00:18:54.340
You lot!

00:18:54.750 --> 00:18:58.010
Zhou, finally we can talk face to face.

00:18:58.220 --> 00:19:00.090
You cannot be here.

00:19:00.380 --> 00:19:03.720
What are you talking about?
It was you who said we should come here.

00:19:04.350 --> 00:19:07.930
Counselor, have you found your ball?

00:19:09.100 --> 00:19:12.400
You took the ball, didn't you?

00:19:14.320 --> 00:19:15.110
What?

00:19:18.150 --> 00:19:20.650
Kyoko! What do you think you're doing?

00:19:20.820 --> 00:19:23.410
He's your enemy!

00:19:25.530 --> 00:19:29.370
Give it back, you damn thief!

00:19:37.090 --> 00:19:38.010
Stop!

00:19:43.300 --> 00:19:45.810
-Oh no...
-You bastard!

00:19:45.970 --> 00:19:48.220
What've you done?

00:19:52.850 --> 00:19:55.730
Is everything all right, Counselor?

00:19:55.900 --> 00:19:58.110
We've gotta get out of here.

00:20:05.660 --> 00:20:06.490
Here.

00:20:07.490 --> 00:20:09.790
I don't get it.

00:20:10.040 --> 00:20:14.880
The counselor's memories were altered
to get him to work for the Company, right?

00:20:15.250 --> 00:20:17.750
If he's dead, all that effort
has gone to waste...

00:20:18.090 --> 00:20:19.340
Satoru.

00:20:19.630 --> 00:20:22.970
Unless you want to join him, I advise you
not to go looking for answers.

00:20:23.220 --> 00:20:24.930
Yes, I know.

00:20:32.520 --> 00:20:33.310
Tsukasa!

00:20:33.480 --> 00:20:36.610
-I'm back.
-Tsukasa! Tsukasa!

00:20:38.070 --> 00:20:39.690
Well done, Hiroki.

00:20:40.940 --> 00:20:43.360
You kept it running.

00:20:43.530 --> 00:20:44.820
Our store.

00:20:45.820 --> 00:20:47.990
Sure did!

00:21:10.930 --> 00:21:13.930
You really think he's capable of
running a store?

00:21:14.100 --> 00:21:15.730
Of course not.

00:21:16.350 --> 00:21:19.150
He's never even lived anywhere
other than a hotel.

00:21:19.360 --> 00:21:21.360
Then why bother?

00:21:21.690 --> 00:21:23.860
It's worth it, Katsuragi.

00:21:24.070 --> 00:21:26.990
I'd do anything for Hiroki.

00:21:27.490 --> 00:21:31.830
When you find a "pet" like that,
you do whatever it takes to keep them.

00:21:32.040 --> 00:21:34.620
Whatever you say.

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:38.250
-Anyway, why does it have to be us?
-What?

00:21:38.710 --> 00:21:42.250
The next job. Can't you and Satoru do it?

00:21:42.590 --> 00:21:45.420
Satoru is a nonstarter for this one,

00:21:45.590 --> 00:21:47.510
because it's about Hayashi.

00:21:48.970 --> 00:21:51.140
Mr. Hayashi has been found?

00:21:51.810 --> 00:21:52.890
He has.

00:21:54.020 --> 00:21:59.020
Seems he wasn't in China at all,
but was holed up here the whole damn time.

00:21:59.400 --> 00:22:02.610
That idiot! He should've known
we'd find him sooner or later!

00:22:03.070 --> 00:22:07.030
You seem strangely happy for someone
who was outwitted for two whole years.

00:22:08.240 --> 00:22:10.450
Hiroki can sit out the Hayashi job.

00:22:10.620 --> 00:22:12.910
You and I will handle it.

00:22:13.330 --> 00:22:14.410
Understood.

00:23:50.090 --> 00:23:55.010
"An Unholy Fusion of Two Chief Editors?"
Artist: Miso Suzuki
